\section{Gradient Boosting (Phases 8B, 8C)}
Boosting fits shallow regression trees to the negative gradient of log loss, $r=y-p$, with Newton leaf values $\sum r/\sum p(1-p)$. Our from-scratch implementation gives the same September log loss (<<d5['scratch_vs_sklearn']['ours (from scratch)']['September log loss']>>) and PR AUC (<<d5['scratch_vs_sklearn']['ours (from scratch)']['September PR AUC']>>) as scikit-learn.

\textbf{The early-stopping trap.} Early-stopping on the month that is then scored lets the stopping rule see the answers. For one fixed configuration this inflated the mean rolling PR AUC from <<f3(hon['mean'])>> to <<f3(opt['mean'])>> (Table~\ref{tab:trap}). Our protocol for month $m$: train on months before $m-1$, early-stop on $m-1$, refit on all months before $m$ with that many trees, and score $m$.

