\section{Results on the Test Months (Phase 9)}
The test months were scored once (Table~\ref{tab:test}, Fig.~\ref{fig:test}). All learned models clearly beat both baselines, and the three learned models' 95\% intervals overlap heavily: the hybrid and logistic regression are practically identical, and boosting is <<f3(LR['pr_auc'] - GB['pr_auc'])>> lower, well inside the interval width. Platt scaling lowered boosting's calibration error but raised logistic regression's and the hybrid's: their maximum-likelihood probabilities were already calibrated, and October's lower base rate pulled them down.

